-might-agree/a-79726190?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Moscow is pushing for a summit with Donald Trump and Xi Jinping to discuss ending the war in Ukraine, without Kyiv or the EU. What does Russia hope to gain, and why might China be willing to take part?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Meta ordered to pay $25 billion in Cambridge Analytica case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6f75d9bd4c23be74a8e2a8768f034ea4df2de9029b1e7bb3340581ff25f7c8d</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:16:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/meta-ordered-to-pay-25-billion-in-cambridge-analytica-case/a-79726486--b8819bb1d1ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/meta-ordered-to-pay-25-billion-in-cambridge-analytica-case/a-79726486?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A New Mexico judge ordered Facebook's parent company, Meta, to pay $25 billion for misleading users over the Cambridge Analytica breach, which took place during Donald Trump's first presidential campaign.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>PHP developers say key patches available after global scare</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ac4fa396ab700b498ae2708c3314a6fcdae40756c31a605d81b9d2a23a206ce</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:16:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T16:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/php-developers-say-key-patches-available-after-global-scare/a-79725938--b79bba717c58.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/php-developers-say-key-patches-available-after-global-scare/a-79725938?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Newly discovered vulnerabilities in the PHP programming language have put millions of websites at risk, with government agencies sounding alarms and taking down sites. Developers say updating systems is "imperative."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Raids at far-right group's offices at European Parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a28def260fd863590b07fd8d19bff02258bc36afdba3c98e910576a70c7eb46f</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:16:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/raids-at-far-right-group-s-offices-at-european-parliament/a-79724631--002ed5188c2e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/raids-at-far-right-group-s-offices-at-european-parliament/a-79724631?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities searched the Patriots for Europe's European Parliament offices in a long-running funding inquiry. The group says the charges pertain to its predecessor and there is "no legal continuity" between the two.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia arrests German man, calls him a Ukraine 'mercenary'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38cf08db19b2ab59fdbb7f351d166360abe8b4ce82ddc73b99ffe1402891ee2c</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-arrests-german-man-calls-him-a-ukraine-mercenary/a-79723871--8b55608360c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-arrests-german-man-calls-him-a-ukraine-mercenary/a-79723871?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russian FSB agents have arrested a German national and accused him of fighting as a mercenary for Ukraine's military. They claim he deserted over unpaid wages and say he was a sniper who once served in the Bundeswehr.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia frees jailed American Stephen Hubbard during Witkoff talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c47bd450918bf3b853b8bf8c64725b55b333f382bcffe076b3ad1a9cffb138a</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T13:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-frees-jailed-american-stephen-hubbard-during-witkoff-talks/a-79719452--b6488d619654.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-frees-jailed-american-stephen-hubbard-during-witkoff-talks/a-79719452?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">During talks between Vladimir Putin and Steve Witkoff, Putin announced that jailed American Stephen Hubbard had been released. The Kremlin also said Russia was "in principle" ready to resume trilateral talks next month.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan-Taliban conflict: How India could benefit from shifting regional dynamics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58d6836816d71c0737b818669747a3cf5168f14913573293027b143e6d40e11a</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-taliban-conflict-how-india-could-benefit-from-shifting-regional-dynamics/a-79721426--f7ab516276cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-taliban-conflict-how-india-could-benefit-from-shifting-regional-dynamics/a-79721426?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Pakistan's influence in Afghanistan comes under strain, India is rebuilding ties with the Taliban in Kabul. Can New Delhi turn this diplomatic opening into lasting strategic gains?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK approves Jackdaw gas field after years in limbo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a333d453ccf3cb906a0cfed507001bb30e2f233ac28e699456631578668885fe</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T09:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-approves-jackdaw-gas-field-after-years-in-limbo/a-79720557--b9a9f932ca8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-approves-jackdaw-gas-field-after-years-in-limbo/a-79720557?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Drilling is set to begin in the controversial North Sea plot as the government seeks to tackle high energy costs. Environmental groups have criticized the move and called for more clean energy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US sanctions target Iran's rail sector as Tehran shifts cargo from sea routes to overland corridors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:daeb09b4f13703bcaafd2f120941e93b521b46aacdac3a82f5e441ac3ed09ed8</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T08:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-sanctions-target-iran-s-rail-sector-as-tehran-shifts-cargo-from-sea-routes-to-overland-corridors/a-79681413--6d742d0c6640.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-sanctions-target-iran-s-rail-sector-as-tehran-shifts-cargo-from-sea-routes-to-overland-corridors/a-79681413?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As US sanctions expand to Iran's rail sector, Tehran is relying more heavily on overland links with China and Central Asia. But capacity constraints, delays and costs limit rail's ability to replace maritime trade.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Australian MP Helen Haines loses both legs after car attack as suspect appears in court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:615c24a3e5a6670b61922209687816dd9ce21511b136d09270c9bcc0cb9542ed</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australian-mp-helen-haines-loses-both-legs-after-car-attack-as-suspect-appears-in-court/a-79697660--bbf1d96427b0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australian-mp-helen-haines-loses-both-legs-after-car-attack-as-suspect-appears-in-court/a-79697660?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Doctors have amputated both of Helen Haines legs after the Australian lawmaker was hit in an apparent deliberate attack. The suspected driver involved in the attack has appeared in court.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Football: German coach Hürzeler flying high in Premier League</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:546944c6fff955773dc8e2c56645be2911d9d3256733c928ba7d5e6223779ae5</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T06:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/football-german-coach-h_rzeler-flying-high-in-premier-league/a-79714763--701507a044eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/football-german-coach-hürzeler-flying-high-in-premier-league/a-79714763?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fabian Hürzeler is younger than his star player, a fellow Premier League German. But, contrary to his reputation in his homeland, Hürzeler has become a popular figure both on and off the pitch in England.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>India news: India-US trade deal 'pretty close,' says Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d68463b094e5bbc85315b4784a20443e8056109942de10223947edefbb74459</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T06:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-india-us-trade-deal-pretty-close-says-trump/live-79719383--cfe288ad80da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-india-us-trade-deal-pretty-close-says-trump/live-79719383?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump hinted that the US-India trade deal could look different from the previous ones.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Musk says SpaceX-Tesla merger 'good idea' as companies explore union</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f225b57eb68c1ed1676b3d4f8add5bdf56575cf828956a03c3e4bac8d646913</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T05:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/musk-says-spacex-tesla-merger-good-idea-as-companies-explore-union/a-79719220--a18c1fbf34a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/musk-says-spacex-tesla-merger-good-idea-as-companies-explore-union/a-79719220?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Musk confirmed the long standing speculation of a possible merger between Tesla and SpaceX but warned that it would be premature to assume it is happening for sure.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>Rising emissions and temperatures: The cost of Trump's climate retreat is now clear</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04ae7f3fad1c0caf0a80450ac54aef106e9f63040d535ce0a494819fbf04e7a1</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T05:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rising-emissions-and-temperatures-the-cost-of-trump-s-climate-retreat-is-now-clear/a-79714915--c58ce7a39bf5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rising-emissions-and-temperatures-the-cost-of-trump-s-climate-retreat-is-now-clear/a-79714915?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The world is set to breach the critical 1.5-degree temperature limit, with Donald Trump's US withdrawal from climate action worsening the outlook, according to a UN report. But there is a small silver lining.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Elon Musk ordered a slowdown of Starlink in Ukraine — report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9edbb28df3a8f937ef2e3aab46137d307df19ff758cdf530500960aeea857c7d</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T03:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/elon-musk-ordered-a-slowdown-of-starlink-in-ukraine-report/a-79718899--f41ab1e64a12.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/elon-musk-ordered-a-slowdown-of-starlink-in-ukraine-report/a-79718899?maca=en-rss-en-t