T22:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afd-s-alice-weidel-to-unveil-plan-to-cut-eu-powers-report/a-79717944--20fa5b0134f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afd-s-alice-weidel-to-unveil-plan-to-cut-eu-powers-report/a-79717944?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right AfD will propose slashing powers of the European Union when it presents its policy paper on Wednesday, Politico reports.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Zelenskyy visits Norway amid Trump White House tensions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7aaca452498dfc81b0eeae2b6e309851bc0f5d0c2219c6344f4b198effd8bfac</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T19:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/zelenskyy-visits-norway-amid-trump-white-house-tensions/a-79717354--f26d4c094394.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/zelenskyy-visits-norway-amid-trump-white-house-tensions/a-79717354?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Zelenskyy met with Norwegian and Finnish leaders in Oslo and held talks with Trump envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner. Trump is pressuring Zelenskyy to "make a deal" with Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria records its first Ebola case, in capital Abuja</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41a924a3530342fad3bcc6ddbb6148ab040bc00137140ecf33f2fcdd8af632f1</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:14:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T19:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-in-capital-abuja/a-79717377--c6985b1c776f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-in-capital-abuja/a-79717377?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nigeria has reported its first known case of Ebola during Africa's latest outbreak originating in the DRC. Health Minister Muhammad Ali Pate said the patient was a woman who had recently flown to Abuja from Uganda.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
